## ---------------------------------------------------------------- discoveries
observer.disc.the_figure.title=The Figure
observer.disc.the_figure.text=Tall. Taller than a door. Black like the space between trees. Two white points where a face should be. It did not move while I looked. When I looked again it was not there.
observer.disc.the_figure.lesson=It does not like to be looked at. Hold your eyes on it and it will step away.
observer.disc.out_of_step.title=Out of Step
observer.disc.out_of_step.text=My footsteps had an echo that matched me exactly. When I stopped, it stopped too. Then it took one more step.
observer.disc.out_of_step.lesson=When the steps behind you stop after you do, turn around. It is there, behind something.
observer.disc.quiet_feet.title=Quiet Feet
observer.disc.quiet_feet.text=I crept instead of walking, and the steps behind me lost their rhythm. They stumbled twice and gave up.
observer.disc.quiet_feet.lesson=It copies your rhythm. Sneak, and it cannot follow you by sound.
observer.disc.someone_was_home.title=Someone Was Home
observer.disc.someone_was_home.text=I came home and things were arranged. Not broken. Arranged. A door I had shut. The lights by the entrance. Something turned toward the way I come in.
observer.disc.someone_was_home.lesson=It visits the place you return to most, just before you return. Look for what changed.
observer.disc.put_back.title=Put Back
observer.disc.put_back.text=I put one thing back the way it was. Later, the rest had been put back too.
observer.disc.put_back.lesson=Answer its changes. Restore one, and it restores the rest.
observer.disc.small_likeness.title=Small Likeness
observer.disc.small_likeness.text=A little figure, burnt black, with two pale points for eyes. It was facing me. When I broke it, there was something left in my hand.
observer.disc.small_likeness.lesson=Effigies mark where it stood. Break them for Vestiges.
observer.disc.something_facing.title=Something Facing You
observer.disc.something_facing.text=It had been facing the wall. Now it faces me. I heard nothing move.
observer.disc.something_facing.lesson=Objects with a front can turn. If one faces you that did not before, it was here.
observer.disc.the_door.title=The Door
observer.disc.the_door.text=I closed the door it opened. Something knocked, once, from the other side.
observer.disc.the_door.lesson=Doors it opens are invitations. Closing them is an answer it accepts.
observer.disc.lights_out.title=Lights Out
observer.disc.lights_out.text=The lights went out one by one, farthest first, as if someone walked toward me putting them out. I lit one again, and it stopped.
observer.disc.lights_out.lesson=When the lights go out in order, it is testing you. Bring light back.
observer.disc.light_it_doesnt_make.title=Light It Does Not Make
observer.disc.light_it_doesnt_make.text=It would not step into my light. It stood at the edge of it and then it was gone.
observer.disc.light_it_doesnt_make.lesson=It will not walk into light it did not make. Bright light (level 11+) drives it back.
observer.disc.held_gaze.title=Held Gaze
observer.disc.held_gaze.text=While I watched it, it did not come closer. The moment I looked away, it was nearer.
observer.disc.held_gaze.lesson=It only advances while unwatched. Keep your eyes on it; hold long enough and it backs away.
observer.disc.behind_left.title=Always the Same Place
observer.disc.behind_left.text=Wherever I go, it stands in the same place relative to me. Behind, and a little to one side. Always the same side. Always the same distance.
observer.disc.behind_left.lesson=It returns to the same relative position. Learn your side, and check it.
observer.disc.borrowed_work.title=Borrowed Work
observer.disc.borrowed_work.text=I heard my own work — the sound of what I do every day — coming from a place I had already left. There was nobody there. There were footprints.
observer.disc.borrowed_work.lesson=It borrows the sounds of your habits. Going to look stops it.
observer.disc.echo_ahead.title=Echo Ahead
observer.disc.echo_ahead.text=Dark motes rose from a place ahead, with a chime. Soon after, it was standing exactly there.
observer.disc.echo_ahead.lesson=The chime and the motes mark where it will be. If you watch the spot, it cannot arrive.
observer.disc.wrong_way.title=Wrong Way
observer.disc.wrong_way.text=The way back was not the way I came. The stone looked right. It had not been there before.
observer.disc.wrong_way.lesson=It changes familiar routes behind you. The new walls break easily, and drop nothing.
observer.disc.breathing_room.title=Breathing Room
observer.disc.breathing_room.text=It ran at me. I ran too. When I could no longer see it, it stopped following.
observer.disc.breathing_room.lesson=When it hunts: watched, it can only walk. Light, water and distance end the chase. Sprinting outruns it.
observer.disc.second_witness.title=Second Witness
observer.disc.second_witness.text=It was not watching me. It was watching someone else, from where only I could see it.
observer.disc.second_witness.lesson=In company, watch each other's backs. Tell them where it is.
observer.disc.while_you_slept.title=While You Slept
observer.disc.while_you_slept.text=I woke to a door open and a little figure at the foot of the bed, and footprints between them.
observer.disc.while_you_slept.lesson=It visits while you sleep. Check your doors when you wake.
observer.disc.elsewhere_too.title=Elsewhere Too
observer.disc.elsewhere_too.text=I left the world I knew. Not long after, something heavy arrived where I came through.
observer.disc.elsewhere_too.lesson=Changing dimension does not lose it. It follows a little later.
observer.disc.the_window.title=The Window
observer.disc.the_window.text=I was inside. It was outside, framed by the window, watching me be inside.
observer.disc.the_window.lesson=Walls are not where it stops. Glance at your windows.
observer.disc.close.title=Close
observer.disc.close.text=Cloth shifting. A slow breath. I turned around and it was right there, its head tilted, as if I were the strange one.
observer.disc.close.lesson=A breath behind you means turn around. Facing it ends the moment without harm.
observer.disc.through_the_lens.title=Through the Lens
observer.disc.through_the_lens.text=I looked at it through the lens and it flinched. When there is nothing to see, the lens shows where it walked.
observer.disc.through_the_lens.lesson=The Witness Lens makes it recoil and withdraw. Use it to read its trails.
observer.msg.vigil_busy=§7Not now. Its attention is on someone else. Try again in a little while.
